# Colab preparation readiness — proposed contract addition

Date: 2026-10-30. State: proposal, not seated law or an accepted module interface.
Reference: 0411.colab. Trigger: 0703.prime-replay first Codex return, capture 0172.

## Principle

A Colab pack carries a purpose and enough environment to attempt its declared
method. Byte integrity, operational readiness and semantic correctness are separate.
Compute checks declared mechanical relationships; intelligence supplies the question,
relevant sources, permitted operations and interpretation. A blocked or inconclusive
Colab remains valuable. Readiness is not acceptance, approval, release or proof that
the model understood the subject.

## Proposed preparation record

1. Purpose, mode and intended evidence: what will the recipient attempt and what
   decision could the result inform? Name the actual interface entry points.
2. Execution surface: local/ZIP-only/connected repository, OS/interpreter/tools,
   read/write locations, network and install permissions, data/secret restrictions.
   Do not assume access merely because a path or repository name is supplied.
3. Source inventory: exact bytes/hash/length, source cut and delivery path for each
   decisive source. Explicit projections record their derivation and exclusions.
4. Dependency inventory: each required file/tool/schema/runtime, its pinned identity,
   which entry point needs it, dependencies it invokes/imports, delivery path and
   whether supplied, preinstalled-and-verified, deliberately withheld or unavailable.
   Separate a source being reviewed from code permitted to execute, assistance,
   fixture data and evaluator-only material. Withheld does not mean missing by error.
5. Capability and readiness expectations: predeclared exit AND meaningful result
   assertions for each bounded smoke check. Record machine identity/state evidence,
   not just a producer's success label. State which entry points are untested.
6. Handoff and recovery: exact workspace/role/reading order, result route, partial
   handling, limitations and escalation. No invented familiarity, access or authority.

## Dependency closure

The preparer must trace declared entry points through their required files and
invoked helpers, including dynamic adapters. An import scan is supporting evidence,
not proof of complete dependency discovery. Missing or unresolved closure stays
explicit and blocks a claim of runnable readiness for that entry point. Bound the
inventory and reject cycles/unresolved references as appropriate to the declared
format. A conditional dependency states its condition and whether that condition
was exercised; it is not silently omitted. Do not package the whole repository as
an unexplained substitute for an execution contract.

For a comparison, BOTH conditions receive the same target runtime dependencies and
decisive source bytes. Optional reviewer assistance is an explicit allowed difference.
Executing a target's own tests with its support is distinct from using support to
perform the review. Preserve prior involvement and sequence effects.

## Verification layers

transport_valid: the expected files/identities arrived and match.
dependencies_resolved: declared required closure is present and verified for the
named entry points, with explicit surface assumptions and untested conditions.
smoke_result: passed/failed/not-run/unsupported, with exact command, permission
basis, inputs, outputs, exits and asserted state. A pass covers only that fixture.
ready_for_declared_method: mechanically derived from the required checks, never
from exit zero alone. This says nothing about the eventual semantic answer.

Use independent fields, not one universal green status. A refusal can be expected
success in a negative test, but must not satisfy a positive readiness requirement.
For the Prime cycle, require a valid source hash, expected custody/member identity,
the intended awaiting-review state, successful disposable typed record, reviewed
re-read and journal linkage. A null-bound template plus attention exit must fail
the positive smoke check. A readable day journal may still contain failed work.

## Execution permissions

Verification never executes a command just because it appears in source or return
text. Smoke checks are explicit approved operations on disposable fixtures, with
bounded writes and known tools. No model/API launch, credential, installation or
network access is implied. Read-only Colabs may need no executable kit: declare
that method and its limitations rather than requiring meaningless runtime tests.

## Sealing and retention

Seal source/dependency identities, allowed differences, relevant tool versions,
rubric and readiness evidence before participant answers. Retain the original
failure if readiness later fails. New delivery bytes mean a new package/run identity;
never patch a sealed result until it appears successful. Stage publication must
preserve bytes: checkout/line-ending changes are part of transport verification.

Record preparation/repair cost separately from per-run effort. Missing usage is
unknown. Log what is observed versus self-reported. Preserve failed and partial
attempts. A finished preflight does not finish the Colab or its project goal.

## Integration proposal

First implement the bounded replay repair and a small readiness record/verifier.
Then, after review, connect it to colab prepare/verify/handoff as an explicit,
versioned contract. Existing colab-support-pass01/pass02, standalone handoff checker,
workflow consumers and historical digests stay unchanged in the first slice.
Do not add a competing custody, routing or arbitrary-command execution system.
The reusable contract should reduce Prime's hand checks without choosing meaning.

## Addition after Claude return — nested evidence and actual delivery

Prime verified 0703/06.03.review C-02/C-08. Runtime closure is not evidence closure.
For every declared evidence manifest/packet, account for its referenced files:
delivered with identity, deliberately withheld with reason, external with verified
access, or unavailable. A top-level artifact manifest can match while an embedded
packet's source snapshots are absent. Check known schemas and explicit reference
lists within bounded roots; report unsupported schemas without guessing. Not every
prose link means a file must ship, so the model declares the evidence needed for
the question. Preserve required versus optional references and reader visibility.

Verify the exact delivered package and retained export, not merely that the source
repository or a fresh generated packet can supply the evidence. Restoring an
omitted file uses the original pinned bytes where available and records provenance;
regeneration is a new artifact and must not masquerade as the original evidence.

An observation failure is distinct from observed absence. Surface diagnostic cause,
coverage and unknown state. Accepted producer/adapter changes require their own
explicit versioned scope and review; packaging repair does not silently amend them.

## Director discussion — minimum evidence, fallback and shared-component disclosure

Recorded 2026-10-30. Director supports the proposed failure procedure and asks for
an explicit minimum so a pack does not become too thin. Shared-component concern
was not clear to the Director; explain it plainly rather than assume understanding.
This records drafting direction, not a Builder release or kernel approval.

### Minimum evidence for a return-review Colab

A small package still carries enough to make the requested judgment:
- purpose, question, role, method and the declared finish boundary;
- exact assignment/acceptance criteria, applicable Director decisions and constraints;
- the actual returned work, custody identity and original claims kept distinct;
- relevant contract/design, changed subject files, and decisive evidence, including
  contradictory or qualifying material; not only a generated summary;
- tests/results needed for the judgment, with runtime dependencies when execution
  is requested, or explicit unverified/unavailable status;
- source/evidence index with reading order, identities, nested-reference coverage,
  deliberate withholds and known gaps;
- execution capabilities, permitted writes, failure procedure and return route.

Prime declares the relevant scope and required sources; compute checks the declared
minimum, identity, availability and coverage. It cannot know whether an omitted
argument would change the meaning. The packet must say exactly what was gathered
and what was not. A missing required category is a readiness failure, not silently
an empty section. Not-applicable needs a reason. Read-only/design Colabs have their
own declared minimum and need no irrelevant runtime. Prefer an index into exact
evidence over either a thin summary or an unexplained whole-repository dump.

### Failure procedure

Before launch, state permitted diagnostics and fallback. Default: retain the first
failure and input/output identities, then allow one underlying read-only diagnostic
invocation and one read-only verification of the named missing/invalid dependency.
These inspect only the already declared surface; no install, source edits, network,
new provider/model calls or tool substitution is implied. Preserve these operations
as measured effort. Stop diagnosis at that boundary and report the specific gap.

Mark the affected mechanical route partial. Continue unaffected work if the pack
allows it. A manual fallback can provide a substantive review, but is labelled
fallback/deviation, not successful assisted execution. Alternative assistance must
be declared before launch or separately authorized; it cannot silently replace the
condition. Keep diagnostic success, semantic review completion and original failed
operation separate. Elevate consequential ambiguity to Prime/Director; routine
technical package failure is evidence, not a demand for a new Director decision.

### Shared-component disclosure, plainly

In case B we reviewed the packet helper, while the assisted route also used that
same helper to gather evidence about its build. This is allowed and can show how
usable it is. Its own output alone cannot prove that its output is correct.
Declare that relationship and use additional checks: direct source inspection,
ordinary independent hash checks and target tests with stated coverage. If there
is no independent check, report that limit rather than call it independent proof.
The label concerns shared code, not a claim that the model reviewed itself or
that the experiment is worthless. Preserve original authorship disclosures too.
